{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '4\\\\.6|4\\\\.7|M0|M1|M2|UNTESTED|output-patches|fallback|duplicate' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; which -a git; cat src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"510:Unavailability does not trigger an undisclosed remote fallback.\n621:### 4.6 The multi-target pipeline and the parse-tree IR\n642:(duplicate edges, DFS preorder, real-token text against source bytes,\n691:- Duplicate identical chunks can be deduplicated; conflicting duplicates\n898:rerun parsing, allocate fresh names, or duplicate diagnostics.\n1029:### 7.3 Derive rather than duplicate\n1399:| fallback, `except*`,                         |                        |                                                                              |\n2688:- Identities duplicate. The child lowers its own copy of each\n3029:- No fallback between frontends: `:yang.python/antlr` and\n3171:  unavailable-parser for that grammar's id with no legacy fallback (amended\n3184:  name-environment entry is refused with no bundled fallback (semantic,\n4019:- Fault injection for service restart, duplicate delivery,\n4095:| Fault               | service restart, duplicate delivery,        |\n/usr/bin/git\n(ns yang.antlr.packet\n  \"The target-neutral parse-tree IR and its reader (docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n   §5.5). ANTLR has no neutral tree: each target materializes its own\n   parse-tree objects. This namespace owns the neutral form every host's\n   exporter produces (`yang.antlr.cst`, one file per host) and every\n   language's CST-to-UAST converter consumes: the CST packet, version 1.\n\n   Packet (version 1):\n\n     {:yang.cst/version 1\n      :yang.cst/unit u\n      :yang.cst/grammar id\n      :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/ok | :yang.cst/syntax-error | :yang.cst/source-error\n      :yang.cst/root 0                       ; ok only\n      :yang.cst/nodes [record ...]           ; ok only, preorder, id = index\n      :yang.cst/errors [error ...]           ; non-ok only\n      :yang.cst/complete true}\n\n   Rule record  {:id n :kind :rule :rule \\\"name\\\" :children [ids] :span [s e]}\n   Token record {:id n :kind :token :type \\\"NAME\\\" :text t :span [s e]}\n                 plus :synthetic true when the token's text is not the source\n                 at its span (indentation helpers, EOF); its span is then\n                 zero-width.\n   Error record {:kind :syntax-error :message m :line l :column c :span [s e]}\n\n   Spans are half-open UTF-8 byte offsets into the sealed source. A unit with\n   any syntax error yields an error packet and no nodes: never a partial\n   program.\n\n   Invariants every target's exporter must meet (`conform` checks 2-5):\n\n     1. ids are preorder indexes; :root is 0; child edges form a tree\n        (`validate!`).\n     2. :rule is the grammar rule name from the parser's rule-name table,\n        never a target class name; :type is the symbolic token name, else the\n        literal name, else the decimal type, \\\"EOF\\\" for EOF.\n     3. :span is half-open UTF-8 byte offsets into the sealed source. Each\n        target converts its own index unit at the boundary (the JVM indexes\n        code points; the JS and Dart streams are opened in code-point mode).\n     4. A token is :synthetic with a zero-width span when its text is not the\n        source at its span or it overlaps the previous real token.\n     5. A rule's span covers its real children only; an empty rule is\n        zero-width.\n     6. Any syntax error yields an error packet with :yang.cst/errors and no\n        nodes.\n     7. :yang.cst/grammar names the grammar revision and tool; the target does\n        not appear in the packet. Target equivalence is the contract.\n\n   Portable and language-agnostic: child edges are data, so the tree is\n   validated before anything walks it.\")\n\n\n(def packet-version 1)\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Source text\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn code-points\n  \"The code points of `s` as a vector of integers.\"\n  [s]\n  #?(:cljd (vec (.-runes ^String s))\n     :clj (mapv long (.toArray (.codePoints ^String s)))\n     :cljs (mapv #(.codePointAt % 0) (js/Array.from s))))\n\n\n(defn utf8-length\n  \"The UTF-8 byte count of one code point.\"\n  [cp]\n  (cond (< cp 0x80) 1\n        (< cp 0x800) 2\n        (< cp 0x10000) 3\n        :else 4))\n\n\n(defn utf8-bytes\n  \"The UTF-8 byte count of a string: span ends are checked against it.\"\n  [s]\n  (reduce + 0 (map utf8-length (code-points s))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Packet construction and the parser stage transform\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn base\n  [grammar-id unit]\n  {:yang.cst/version packet-version,\n   :yang.cst/unit unit,\n   :yang.cst/grammar grammar-id,\n   :yang.cst/complete true})\n\n\n(defn source-error\n  [grammar-id unit message data]\n  (assoc (base grammar-id unit)\n         :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/source-error\n         :yang.cst/errors [(merge {:kind :source-error, :message message}\n                                  data)]))\n\n\n(defn transform\n  \"The parser stage's transform over source events: chunks accumulate per\n   unit by ordinal; a seal with every chunk present assembles the snapshot,\n   parses it with `parse-unit` (fn [worker unit source] packet), and emits\n   one packet on port `:cst`. A conflicting duplicate chunk, a seal with\n   chunks missing, or an unknown event emits a source-error packet instead.\n   State is `{unit {ordinal text}}`.\"\n  [parse-unit worker]\n  (let [grammar-id (get-in worker [:profile :grammar-id])]\n    (fn [units event]\n      (let [unit (:yang.source/unit event)]\n        (case (:yang.source/event event)\n          :yang.source/chunk\n          (let [ordinal (:yang.source/ordinal event)\n                text (:yang.source/text event)\n                prior (get-in units [unit ordinal])]\n            (if (and (some? prior) (not= prior text))\n              [(dissoc units unit)\n               [[:cst (source-error grammar-id unit \"Conflicting duplicate chunk\"\n                                    {:ordinal ordinal})]]]\n              [(assoc-in units [unit ordinal] text) []]))\n\n          :yang.source/seal\n          (let [chunks (get units unit {})\n                n (:yang.source/chunk-count event)]\n            (if (= (set (range n)) (set (keys chunks)))\n              [(dissoc units unit)\n               [[:cst (parse-unit worker unit\n                                  (apply str (map chunks (range n))))]]]\n              [(dissoc units unit)\n               [[:cst (source-error grammar-id unit \"Seal with missing chunks\"\n                                    {:chunk-count n,\n                                     :present (vec (sort (keys chunks)))})]]]))\n\n          [units\n           [[:cst (source-error grammar-id unit \"Unknown source event\"\n                                {:event (:yang.source/event event)})]]])))))\n\n\n(defn- malformed!\n  [message data]\n  (throw (ex-info message\n                  (merge {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic\n                          :yang.python.antlr/malformed-cst}\n                         data))))\n\n\n(defn validate!\n  \"Return the packet when its nodes form one tree rooted at 0 with preorder\n   ids equal to their index and every child referenced exactly once, after\n   its parent; otherwise throw a qualified malformed-cst error.\"\n  [packet]\n  (let [nodes (:yang.cst/nodes packet)\n        n (count nodes)]\n    (when-not (and (vector? nodes) (pos? n) (= 0 (:yang.cst/root packet)))\n      (malformed! \"CST packet has no root\" {}))\n    (loop [i 0\n           seen #{}]\n      (if (< i n)\n        (let [node (nth nodes i)\n              kids (:children node)]\n          (when-not (= i (:id node))\n            (malformed! \"CST node id is not its index\" {:index i}))\n          (when-not (contains? #{:rule :token} (:kind node))\n            (malformed! \"CST node has an unknown kind\" {:id i}))\n          (doseq [k kids]\n            (when-not (and (integer? k) (< i k n) (not (contains? seen k)))\n              (malformed! \"CST child edge is not a tree edge\"\n                          {:parent i, :child k})))\n          (recur (inc i) (into seen kids)))\n        (when-not (= (dec n) (count seen))\n          (malformed! \"CST has nodes unreachable from the root\"\n                      {:reachable (count seen), :nodes n}))))\n    packet))\n\n\n(defn node\n  [packet id]\n  (nth (:yang.cst/nodes packet) id))\n\n\n(defn root\n  [packet]\n  (node packet (:yang.cst/root packet)))\n\n\n(defn children\n  [packet n]\n  (mapv #(node packet %) (:children n)))\n\n\n(defn rule?\n  ([n] (= :rule (:kind n)))\n  ([n rule-name] (and (= :rule (:kind n)) (= rule-name (:rule n)))))\n\n\n(defn token?\n  ([n] (= :token (:kind n)))\n  ([n text] (and (= :token (:kind n)) (= text (:text n)))))\n\n\n(defn child-rules\n  \"The rule children of `n` named `rule-name`, in order.\"\n  [packet n rule-name]\n  (filterv #(rule? % rule-name) (children packet n)))\n\n\n(defn has-token?\n  [packet n text]\n  (boolean (some #(token? % text) (children packet n))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Conformance (invariants 3-5), the per-target oracle\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn conform\n  \"Check an ok packet against its `source` text; return a vector of\n   violations (empty when it conforms). Spans stay inside [0, utf8 length],\n   are ordered, synthetic tokens are zero-width, real tokens do not overlap\n   the previous real token, and a rule's span covers its real children.\"\n  [packet source]\n  (let [total (utf8-bytes source)\n        nodes (:yang.cst/nodes packet)\n        bad (volatile! [])\n        note! (fn [id why] (vswap! bad conj {:id id, :violation why}))\n        last-end (volatile! 0)]\n    (doseq [n nodes\n            :let [id (:id n)\n                  [a b] (:span n)]]\n      (when-not (and (integer? a) (integer? b) (<= 0 a b total))\n        (note! id :span-out-of-range))\n      (when (= :token (:kind n))\n        (if (:synthetic n)\n          (when-not (= a b) (note! id :synthetic-not-zero-width))\n          (do (when (< a @last-end) (note! id :token-overlaps-previous))\n              (when (and (integer? b) (< a b)) (vreset! last-end b))))))\n    (doseq [n nodes\n            :when (= :rule (:kind n))\n            :let [real (keep (fn [k]\n                               (let [c (nth nodes k)\n                                     [a b] (:span c)]\n                                 (when (and (not (:synthetic c)) (< a b))\n                                   [a b])))\n                             (:children n))\n                  [a b] (:span n)]]\n      (when (and (seq real)\n                 (not= [a b] [(apply min (map first real))\n                              (apply max (map second real))]))\n        (note! (:id n) :rule-span-not-children))\n      (when (and (empty? real) (not= a b))\n        (note! (:id n) :empty-rule-not-zero-width)))\n    @bad))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/yang/antlr/export.cljc src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/yang/antlr/export.cljc src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj'","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.antlr.export\n  \"The host-free half of a CST exporter (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §5.5): the\n   byte-offset table, the token and rule records, the synthetic-token rule\n   and the error record. A host's `yang.antlr.cst` walks its own parse-tree\n   objects through a small `ops` map and gets back the portable nodes:\n\n     {:token?    (fn [node] bool)           ; a terminal node\n      :token     (fn [node] {:type-name s :start i :stop i :text s})\n      :rule-name (fn [ctx] string)\n      :children  (fn [ctx] vector)\n      :start     (fn [ctx] start-index or nil)}\n\n   Indexes are code-point indexes into the source, the unit all three\n   targets use.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.antlr.packet :as packet]))\n\n\n(defn byte-offsets\n  \"Byte offset of each code point index of `cps`, plus the total at index n.\"\n  [cps]\n  (loop [out [0]\n         acc 0\n         cps (seq cps)]\n    (if cps\n      (let [cp (first cps)\n            acc (+ acc (packet/utf8-length cp))]\n        (recur (conj out acc) acc (next cps)))\n      out)))\n\n\n(defn offset-at\n  [offsets i]\n  (nth offsets (max 0 (min i (dec (count offsets))))))\n\n\n(defn token-span\n  \"The byte span of a token's code point range [start, stop]; a token whose\n   stop precedes its start is zero-width.\"\n  [offsets start stop]\n  (let [s (offset-at offsets start)]\n    [s (if (< stop start) s (offset-at offsets (inc stop)))]))\n\n\n(defn syntax-error\n  [message line column span]\n  {:kind :syntax-error, :message (str message), :line line, :column column,\n   :span span})\n\n\n(defn- token-record\n  \"`last-stop` is the stop index of the previous real token: a token that\n   overlaps it was produced by a helper, not read from the source (the\n   Python helper's DEDENT reports the newline it follows as its text).\"\n  [cps offsets last-stop id {:keys [type-name start stop text]}]\n  (let [n (dec (count offsets))\n        real-text (when (and (<= 0 start) (<= start stop) (< stop n))\n                    (subvec cps start (inc stop)))\n        synthetic? (or (not= real-text (some-> text packet/code-points))\n                       (<= start last-stop))\n        span (if synthetic?\n               (let [p (offset-at offsets (inc stop))] [p p])\n               [(offset-at offsets start) (offset-at offsets (inc stop))])]\n    (cond-> {:id id, :kind :token, :type type-name, :text text, :span span}\n      synthetic? (assoc :synthetic true))))\n\n\n(defn export-nodes\n  \"Preorder records for the parse tree under `root`; a record's id is its\n   index.\"\n  [ops cps offsets root]\n  (let [out (volatile! [])\n        last-stop (volatile! -1)]\n    (letfn [(walk\n              [t]\n              (let [id (count @out)]\n                (if ((:token? ops) t)\n                  (let [tok ((:token ops) t)\n                        record (token-record cps offsets @last-stop id tok)]\n                    (when-not (:synthetic record)\n                      (vreset! last-stop (:stop tok)))\n                    (vswap! out conj record))\n                  (do\n                    (vswap! out conj nil)\n                    (let [kids (mapv walk ((:children ops) t))\n                          records @out\n                          ;; a rule covers its real text: synthetic tokens\n                          ;; and empty rules do not stretch it\n                          child-spans (keep (fn [k]\n                                              (let [r (nth records k)\n                                                    [a b] (:span r)]\n                                                (when (and (not (:synthetic r))\n                                                           (< a b))\n                                                  [a b])))\n                                            kids)\n                          start ((:start ops) t)\n                          s (if start (offset-at offsets start) 0)\n                          span (if (seq child-spans)\n                                 [(apply min (map first child-spans))\n                                  (apply max (map second child-spans))]\n                                 [s s])]\n                      (vswap! out assoc id\n                              {:id id,\n                               :kind :rule,\n                               :rule ((:rule-name ops) t),\n                               :children kids,\n                               :span span}))))\n                id))]\n      (walk root)\n      @out)))\n\n\n(defn result\n  \"The packet for a parse: an error packet when `errors` is non-empty.\"\n  [profile unit errors nodes]\n  (let [base (packet/base (:grammar-id profile) unit)]\n    (if (seq errors)\n      (assoc base\n             :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/syntax-error\n             :yang.cst/errors errors)\n      (assoc base\n             :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/ok\n             :yang.cst/root 0\n             :yang.cst/nodes (nodes)))))\n\n\n(defn failure-kind\n  \"Classify a parse's first failure. `failure` is nil (the parse had none),\n   :lexical (a lexer error, which has no token), or the index of the failing\n   token; `real-tokens` are the buffered non-EOF tokens as\n   {:index :start :stop}. End-of-input tokens are EOF and the zero-width ones\n   after the last token with source text (the lexer's EOF can carry a span,\n   so it is excluded by type). Only a failure there is mendable by more\n   input: :end; any earlier failure is :early.\"\n  [failure real-tokens]\n  (let [last-real (reduce max -1\n                          (keep (fn [{:keys [index start stop]}]\n                                  (when (<= start stop) index))\n                                real-tokens))]\n    (cond\n      (nil? failure) nil\n      (and (integer? failure) (> failure last-real)) :end\n      :else :early)))\n(ns yang.antlr.cst\n  \"The host parser interpreter's generic half (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §4.3,\n   §5.1, §5.5): assemble sealed source units, parse each with an ANTLR\n   grammar profile, and export one portable CST packet per unit.\n\n   Nothing here knows a language. A grammar profile supplies the host\n   constructors:\n\n     {:grammar-id  string naming grammar revision and tool\n      :make-lexer  (fn [CharStream] Lexer)\n      :make-parser (fn [TokenStream] Parser)\n      :start       (fn [Parser] ParserRuleContext)}\n\n   No ANTLR object leaves this namespace: a packet is plain data, in the\n   target-neutral shape `yang.antlr.packet` owns (the IR). The host-free half\n   of the export lives in `yang.antlr.export`; this file holds the JVM walk.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.antlr.export :as export]\n    [yang.antlr.packet :as packet])\n  (:import\n    (org.antlr.v4.runtime\n      ANTLRErrorListener\n      BaseErrorListener\n      CharStreams\n      CommonTokenStream\n      Lexer\n      NoViableAltException\n      Parser\n      ParserRuleContext\n      Recognizer\n      Token)\n    (org.antlr.v4.runtime.atn\n      ATN\n      LexerATNSimulator\n      ParserATNSimulator\n      PredictionContextCache)\n    (org.antlr.v4.runtime.dfa\n      DFA)\n    (org.antlr.v4.runtime.tree\n      TerminalNode)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Worker: exclusively owned recognizer caches (§4.3)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- fresh-dfa\n  ^\"[Lorg.antlr.v4.runtime.dfa.DFA;\" [^ATN atn]\n  (into-array DFA\n              (map (fn [i] (DFA. (.getDecisionState atn i) i))\n                   (range (.getNumberOfDecisions atn)))))\n\n\n(defn make-worker\n  \"A host worker for `profile` owning its own DFA and prediction-context\n   caches, so no parse shares mutable recognizer state with another worker.\n   The worker is host state owned by one parser stage; it is not data and\n   never crosses a stream.\"\n  [profile]\n  (let [lexer ^Lexer ((:make-lexer profile) (CharStreams/fromString \"\"))\n        parser ^Parser ((:make-parser profile)\n                        (CommonTokenStream. lexer))\n        lexer-atn (.getATN lexer)\n        parser-atn (.getATN parser)]\n    {:profile profile,\n     :lexer-atn lexer-atn,\n     :lexer-dfa (fresh-dfa lexer-atn),\n     :lexer-cache (PredictionContextCache.),\n     :parser-atn parser-atn,\n     :parser-dfa (fresh-dfa parser-atn),\n     :parser-cache (PredictionContextCache.)}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Export\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- error-listener\n  \"Collects syntax errors as data into `errors` (a volatile).\"\n  [errors offsets]\n  (proxy [BaseErrorListener] []\n    (syntaxError\n      [^Recognizer recognizer offending line column msg _e]\n      (let [span (if (instance? Token offending)\n                   (let [^Token t offending]\n                     (export/token-span offsets (.getStartIndex t)\n                                        (.getStopIndex t)))\n                   (if (instance? Lexer recognizer)\n                     (let [^Lexer lx recognizer]\n                       [(export/offset-at offsets (._tokenStartCharIndex lx))\n                        (export/offset-at offsets\n                                          (.index (.getInputStream lx)))])\n                     nil))]\n        (vswap! errors conj (export/syntax-error msg line column span))))))\n\n\n(defn- ops\n  [^Parser parser]\n  (let [rule-names (.getRuleNames parser)\n        vocab (.getVocabulary parser)]\n    {:token? (fn [t] (instance? TerminalNode t)),\n     :token (fn [t]\n              (let [tok (.getSymbol ^TerminalNode t)\n                    type (.getType tok)]\n                {:type-name (if (= type Token/EOF)\n                              \"EOF\"\n                              (or (.getSymbolicName vocab type)\n                                  (.getLiteralName vocab type)\n                                  (str type))),\n                 :start (.getStartIndex tok),\n                 :stop (.getStopIndex tok),\n                 :text (.getText tok)})),\n     :rule-name (fn [ctx]\n                  (aget rule-names (.getRuleIndex ^ParserRuleContext ctx))),\n     :children (fn [^ParserRuleContext ctx]\n                 (mapv #(.getChild ctx (int %))\n                       (range (.getChildCount ctx)))),\n     :start (fn [^ParserRuleContext ctx]\n              (some-> (.getStart ctx)\n                      (.getStartIndex)))}))\n\n\n(defn parse-unit\n  \"Parse one sealed unit's `source` with `worker`; return its CST packet.\"\n  [worker unit ^String source]\n  (let [{:keys [profile]} worker\n        cps (packet/code-points source)\n        offsets (export/byte-offsets cps)\n        errors (volatile! [])\n        listener (error-listener errors offsets)\n        lexer ^Lexer ((:make-lexer profile) (CharStreams/fromString source))\n        _ (.setInterpreter lexer\n                           (LexerATNSimulator. lexer\n                                               ^ATN (:lexer-atn worker)\n                                               ^\"[Lorg.antlr.v4.runtime.dfa.DFA;\"\n                                               (:lexer-dfa worker)\n                                               ^PredictionContextCache\n                                               (:lexer-cache worker)))\n        _ (.removeErrorListeners lexer)\n        _ (.addErrorListener lexer listener)\n        parser ^Parser ((:make-parser profile) (CommonTokenStream. lexer))\n        _ (.setInterpreter parser\n                           (ParserATNSimulator. parser\n                                                ^ATN (:parser-atn worker)\n                                                ^\"[Lorg.antlr.v4.runtime.dfa.DFA;\"\n                                                (:parser-dfa worker)\n                                                ^PredictionContextCache\n                                                (:parser-cache worker)))\n        _ (.removeErrorListeners parser)\n        _ (.addErrorListener parser listener)\n        tree ((:start profile) parser)]\n    (export/result profile unit @errors\n                   #(export/export-nodes (ops parser) cps offsets tree))))\n\n\n(defn parse-transform\n  \"The parser stage's transform over source events (`packet/transform`).\"\n  [worker]\n  (packet/transform parse-unit worker))\n\n\n(defn utf8-bytes\n  \"The UTF-8 byte count of a string: span ends are checked against it.\"\n  [^String s]\n  (packet/utf8-bytes s))\n\n\n(defn first-failure\n  \"Where the grammar first refuses `source` with `worker`: nil when it\n   parses, `:end` when the first error failed on an end-of-input token, else\n   `:early` (`export/failure-kind` decides).\n\n   The failing token is the offending token of a mismatch; a\n   no-viable-alternative error names the token its prediction began at, so\n   for it the failing token is the furthest one the parser had buffered when\n   the error was reported. A lexer error has no token.\"\n  [worker source]\n  (let [{:keys [profile lexer-atn lexer-dfa lexer-cache parser-atn\n                parser-dfa parser-cache]}\n        worker\n        failure (volatile! nil)\n        lexer ^Lexer ((:make-lexer profile) (CharStreams/fromString source))\n        tokens (CommonTokenStream. lexer)\n        listener (proxy [BaseErrorListener] []\n                   (syntaxError\n                     [_recognizer offending _line _column _msg e]\n                     (when-not @failure\n                       (vreset! failure\n                                (cond\n                                  (not (instance? Token offending)) :lexical\n                                  (instance? NoViableAltException e)\n                                  (dec (count (.get