yet for\" tname \"; record these:\")\n      (pprint/pprint digests))))\n\n\n(defn generate!\n  [only-target]\n  (let [m (read-manifest)\n        src-dir (fetch-grammar! m)]\n    (doseq [t (sort-by key (:targets m))\n            :when (or (nil? only-target) (= only-target (name (key t))))]\n      (generate-target! m src-dir t))))\n\n\n(defn discover!\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [grammar]} (read-manifest)\n        url (str \"https://api.github.com/repos/\" (:repo grammar)\n                 \"/commits?per_page=1&path=\" (:path grammar))\n        body (String. (http-get-bytes url) \"UTF-8\")]\n    (println (re-find #\"\\\"sha\\\":\\s*\\\"[0-9a-f]{40}\\\"\" body))\n    (println (re-find #\"\\\"date\\\":\\s*\\\"[^\\\"]+\\\"\" body))\n    (doseq [dir [(:path grammar) (str (:path grammar) \"/Java\")]]\n      (let [url (str \"https://api.github.com/repos/\" (:repo grammar)\n                     \"/contents/\" dir\n                     (when (:revision grammar)\n                       (str \"?ref=\" (:revision grammar))))\n            listing (String. (http-get-bytes url) \"UTF-8\")]\n        (println dir (mapv second (re-seq #\"\\\"path\\\":\\s*\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"\"\n                                          listing)))))))\n\n\n(defn- arg-value\n  [args flag]\n  (second (drop-while #(not= flag %) args)))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& args]\n  (let [only-target (arg-value args \"--target\")\n        grammars (if-let [g (arg-value args \"--grammar\")]\n                   [g]\n                   (sort (for [d (.listFiles (io/file \"antlr\"))\n                               :when (.exists (io/file d \"manifest.edn\"))]\n                           (.getName d))))]\n    (doseq [g grammars]\n      (binding [*grammar* g]\n        (if (= \"discover\" (first args)) (discover!) (generate! only-target)))))\n  (shutdown-agents))\ndiff --git a/docs/design/yang.antlr.md b/docs/design/yang.antlr.md\nindex ed188169..ffd93ba8 100644\n--- a/docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n+++ b/docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n@@ -491,10 +491,11 @@ The proposed deployment policy is:\n |               | in a worker; TypeScript       | service                  |\n |               | compiled at build             |                          |\n +---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\n-| Dart / CLJD   | Optional generated Dart       | Sidecar where supported, |\n-|               | parser in an isolate          | or a remote service;     |\n-|               |                               | otherwise unsupported    |\n-|               |                               | outcome                  |\n+| Dart / CLJD   | Generated Dart parser (the    | Sidecar where supported, |\n+|               | local implementation for      | or a remote service;     |\n+|               | Python since 2026-10-17; a    | otherwise unsupported    |\n+|               | grammar without a Dart helper | outcome                  |\n+|               | answers `unavailable-parser`) |                          |\n +---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\n ```\n \n@@ -775,6 +776,13 @@ The syntax exporter emits a versioned packet containing:\n - Explicit recovery/error records where applicable.\n - A completion record identifying the complete packet.\n \n+Amended 2026-10-17: `src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc` owns the v1 packet\n+shape (the normative statement and `packet/conform`, the per-target\n+conformance check over the invariants), and `yang.antlr.cst` has one\n+exporter per host (JVM, Node, Dart) over the same profile contract; the\n+packet is the target-neutral parse-tree IR every exporter produces and every\n+language's CST-to-UAST converter consumes.\n+\n CST identifiers are deterministic within a packet, for example preorder\n ordinals. They are not ANTLR object identities.\n \n@@ -3147,17 +3155,22 @@ Linker prerequisites, the linker seat's to build:\n +-------+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n ```\n \n-Acceptance, each on all three hosts unless stated (Node and Dart consume\n-precompiled CST packets or rows, since the parser is JVM-only):\n+Acceptance, each on all three hosts unless stated (amended 2026-10-17: the\n+Python parser is generated for all three hosts, so the session scenarios run\n+through the installed parser on each, and the precompiled packets are checked\n+against it by the packet-parity test; per-target helper availability, 4.2,\n+decides the host matrix of any other grammar):\n \n - F1: two revisions of one id installed into an empty catalog are both\n   selectable and the original catalog is unchanged; a manifest holding a\n   function is rejected with a qualified outcome.\n - F2: a toy frontend defined in a test namespace installs, is selected,\n   and evaluates on every VM with no `src` edit; a newer revision\n-  installed under a live session leaves it unchanged; on Node and Dart\n-  with no parser or configured service, the ANTLR id answers\n-  unavailable-parser with no legacy fallback.\n+  installed under a live session leaves it unchanged; a host with no\n+  generated parser for a grammar, and no configured service, answers\n+  unavailable-parser for that grammar's id with no legacy fallback (amended\n+  2026-10-17: the Python grammar is generated for JVM, Node and Dart, so\n+  `:yang.python/antlr` is installed on every host).\n - P1: the full corpus output is unchanged on every VM and host; a\n   composition with no cell module halts ok on `functions-uast`;\n   `py/init!` twice yields one set of class cells; shadowing then\nname: datomworld_cljd\ndescription: ClojureDart experiment for Datomworld\npublish_to: 'none'\nenvironment:\n  # cbor 6.5.1 (the dao.stream.cbor Dart codec) requires >=3.7.0.\n  sdk: \">=3.7.0 <4.0.0\"\n\ndependencies:\n  flutter:\n    sdk: flutter\n  flutter_gpu:\n    sdk: flutter\n  http: ^1.2.0\n  cbor: 6.5.1\n  crypto: 3.0.7\n  # The :cljd NFC seam (yin.vm.debruijn's normalize-nfc). Pinned to the\n  # Unicode 16.0 release the de Bruijn projection design settled on\n  # 2026-09-21; 0.3.2 moved to Unicode 17.0.\n  unorm_dart: 0.3.1+1\n  # The generated Python3 ANTLR parser (antlr/python3/manifest.edn) runs on\n  # this runtime; one release with the ANTLR tool in deps.edn :antlr-gen.\n  antlr4: 4.13.2\n  # DaoJing multihash content-addressing (BLAKE3).\n  blake3_dart: 1.0.0\n  ed25519_edwards: 0.3.2\n\ndev_dependencies:\n  flutter_test:\n    sdk: flutter\n  test: ^1.29.0\n\nflutter:\n  assets:\n    - assets/shaders/simple_mesh.shaderbundle\n    - assets/images/earth_land_ocean_ice_2048.jpg\n    - assets/images/moon_texture_1024.jpg\n    - assets/images/earth_land_ocean_ice_1024.jpg\n    - assets/images/moon_texture_512.jpg\n{\n  \"name\": \"datomworld\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.1\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"shadow-cljs\": \"3.3.5\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@codemirror/lang-php\": \"^6.0.2\",\n    \"@codemirror/lang-python\": \"^6.2.1\",\n    \"@codemirror/theme-one-dark\": \"^6.1.3\",\n    \"@nextjournal/lang-clojure\": \"^1.0.0\",\n    \"@noble/hashes\": \"2.4.0\",\n    \"antlr4\": \"4.13.2\",\n    \"codemirror\": \"^6.0.2\",\n    \"ol\": \"^6.6.1\",\n    \"punycode\": \"^2.3.1\",\n    \"react\": \"^17.0.2\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"^17.0.2\",\n    \"ws\": \"^8.18.0\"\n  },\n  \"description\": \"A world built on data\",\n  \"main\": \"index.js\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"echo \\\"Error: no test specified\\\" && exit 1\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [],\n  \"author\": \"\",\n  \"license\": \"SEE LICENSE IN LICENSE-EXCEPTION\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
